/ A random table with a column of (nearly) every data type, built from `?`
/ (roll), string vectors and casts. Values change on every run.
/ Each `zip` value is one noun, so a compound expression goes in parens; a cast
/ at the top of a value is applied to that column, so it keeps its final dtype.
n: 5000

/ a timestamp list (raw ns since the epoch, cast); the date and time columns
/ are cast from it below. (Not named `ts`: a global shadows a column of the
/ same name in a query.)
stamps: `timestamp$((1700000000 + n ? 100000000) * 1000000000)

t: zip `id`i8`i32`px`f32`flag`sym`cat`str`ts`day`tm`span!
    (til n)
    (i8$n ? 100)
    (i32$n ? 100000)
    (n ? 500.0)
    (f32$n ? 1.0)
    (n ? 01b)
    (n ? `buy`sell`hold)
    (`$n ? `red`green`blue)
    (n ? ("alpha" "beta" "gamma" "delta"))
    stamps
    (`date$stamps)
    (`time$stamps)
    (`timespan$((n ? 1000) * 1000000))

/ show every column rather than eliding the middle ones
.qpl.cfg maxcol=20 tblwidth=200
t
cols t
